      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T18:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we are abusing `Objects.requireNonNull`.\n\nAs we are calling a method on this object, we would get a NPE if bluetoothManager was null, \n\nFrom the `Objects.requireNonNull` documentation https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/Objects.html#requireNonNull-T-\n\n\nThis method is designed primarily for doing parameter validation in methods and constructors, as demonstrated below:\n```\n public Foo(Bar bar) {\n     this.bar \u003d Objects.requireNonNull(bar);\n }\n```\n\nAnd we are not in this case.\n\nI think that we should remove it and just put\n\n\n```\n        mAdapter \u003d bluetoothManager.getAdapter();\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "47ed493463624d0a645d26c25ca5455e9c9612f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
